      "writtenOn": "2024-03-18T18:32:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We covered this briefly in our meeting but the class hierarchy needs to be cleaned up here.\n\nWe started with a two-tier hierarchy: `DebugTrace` is meant to be our abstract base class, and `DebugTracePriv` was designed to be the implementation of that base.\n\nThis CL puts additional virtual methods in `DebugTracePriv` and moves the implementations to a new _third_ class, `DebugTraceImpl`. That\u0027s unnecessarily complex.\n\nSince `DebugTrace` was designed to be a pure abstract base, let\u0027s move all the virtual methods into `DebugTrace` and mark them as `\u003d 0` pure methods.\n\nWe now need two implementations of `DebugTrace`, one which is real and one which is a no-op stub.\n\n`DebugTracePriv` was designed to be the implementation class, so let\u0027s keep the implementation in there; all your changes can go away except some methods will now be marked `override`.\n\nThen, create a new `DebugTraceStub` class which implements a no-op version of `DebugTrace`.\n\nThen we will once again have an abstract base class, but now with two concrete implementations instead of one.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 68,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 68,
        "endChar": 56
      },
      "revId": "7503f08b915bbb8cd84f466f8075835874af493b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
